Step one, head to the beach to pry open oysters;
Step two, crack open the oysters to find a Water-Repelling Pearl within;
Step three, sell the Water-Repelling Pearl at Seafarer's Alley—instant riches!

Appendix: The Water-Repelling Pearl is an ancient and wondrous treasure. Legend holds that whoever possesses it may walk through water as though treading upon level ground, and it is often regarded as a wondrous object for subduing floods and calming waters. Some say this pearl is born of the Neidan of aquatic creatures, others that it forms from the eyes of dragon-fish—the tales vary and none agree.

Chirping Stream
By Wang Wei, Tang Dynasty

Sweet osmanthus blooms fall unenjoyed;
Vague hills dissolve into night void.
The moonrise startles birds to sing;
Their twitters fill the dale with spring.

A vision spanning thirty years for lasting peace and prosperity:

First, to unify the realm, so the people live free from war and exile; 
Second, to restore livelihoods, banishing famine and hardship; 
Third, to secure homes and lives, allowing all to flourish in safety and joy.
Together: Ten years to expand the lands, ten years to heal the people, and ten years to secure enduring peace!

New hairstyle is available for a limited time.
Drifting ripples trace the dreams of fish;
Soft rain washes spring from fading youth.

